      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Tested ACK 74135e2e625030b18daf7539bd19dabb75948af1. This finishes the fix from #36791: every wait that returns on an event the test triggers now has at least a minute, so none of them can time out on a slow host with the default timeout factor. I checked that the test passes normally, with the faketime command from #36791, and with `sleep_time=1.2` on the `template6` wait, which failed before.\n\nThe waits still using `default_ipc_timeout` (`template4`, `template5` and the two `waitNext` policy tests) are fine as they are: the fees they wait for are already in the mempool, and `waitNext` always checks fees once after its first one-second tick, however short the timeout.",
